 an actor for over 40 years he has a  pretty good idea of what he would be  doing now if Hollywood hadn't worked out  for him when Men's Journal asked him  what he would do if acting weren't an  option he was quick to answer saying I'd  be a carpenter I tried to do that but I  just couldn't get hired like his  character Gibbs who builds boats in his  free time Harmon says he still enjoys  carpentry but he doesn't have much time  to do it anymore when working as a  carpenter didn't pan out for harm and he  went on to work at an ad firm where he  stayed for about four years it was  during this time that he got a promotion  at a sales rep company meaning he was  essentially a shoe salesman for a few  months he recalled the moment he made  the decision to switch to acting  full-time on the flight home after a  work trip in Boston he was sitting next  to a 33 year old man who was telling him  about how he was trying to make pension  by 65 meaning he would have to remain at  his job for another three decades as  Harmon recalled he was drinking his  second Martini by the time we were  wheels up he was miserable in his job  and he was trying to maintain the job  for another another 32 years I went home  got in my car drove out to the place  where I worked and gave my notice  [Music]
 

